Band Description

Copper Breath Registry is a five-member acoustic-electronic ensemble built around the principle that continuous airflow can remain structurally stable while drums, bass, and harmony repeatedly fracture around it.

Maialen Etxeberria — alboka, circular breathing, fingering cells, reed beating, Breath Knot phrasing.

Rowan Pike — halftime drums, sampler, sub architecture, Breath Knot arrangement.

Leire Aranburu — prepared celesta, fixed-pitch proof tones, dry harmonic replies.

Iker Salazar — tamboril, acoustic transient exchange, muted rolls, rim articulation.

Naomi Clarke — contrabass clarinet, low acoustic windows, breath fundamentals, key noise.

There is no conventional frontperson. Maialen maintains the continuous air line, Rowan removes and restores the electronic floor around it, Leire fixes selected pitch centers after fingering shifts, Iker replaces machine transients with taut acoustic strikes, and Naomi occupies the lowest acoustic spaces. Live versions vary because circular-breath timing and reed resistance alter the duration of every TURN and LOCK.

